## 3. The scout's acceptance, in the audit

The four box values are compared against **`ModesSave.profile(store)`'s own career group** and
against **`UiData.profile_summary`**, in the same test, on a career the audit itself wrote
(7/3/2/5 → the fourth box must read `70%`). No expectation in that block is hand-copied from
the screen.

## 4. Capture states, defined here

- `default` — the live career and season.
- `empty-objectives` — the reference's own empty branch (`js/ui.js:1639`): the list shows
  `profileNoObjectives` and zero rows. Asserted, then reverted.
- `mid-season` — pinned progress: the live season's `seasonProgress` with its first pending
  objective's metric brought to that objective's target, so the page shows one done row and at
  least one still open. Asserted both ways.

## 5. Seams recorded, nothing edited outside this ticket

- **`ModesSave.profile()` / `load_career()` / `UiData.season_objectives()` are read-only calls**;
  the audit builds its career through `ModesSave.save_career` inside
  `user://uir16-profile-audit` and removes the directory. The real `user://save` is untouched.
- **Theme tokens**: shares the 15-row request in `uir-13-screen-help.log` §3 (this screen's own
  new names: `win_green`, `stat_muted`, `trophy_yellow`, `white`, `summary_fill`; everything
  else it names – `gold`, `green`, `cyan`, `ink`, `muted`, `line` – already exists).
  **Resolved 2026-09-17 (wave 3):** every one of these rows is in `padel_theme.tres`,
  `theme/README.md` §3 and `theme_probe.gd` — see `uir-wave3-shared-seams.log` §1.
- **Focusables**: back + `profile/unlocks-challenges`; `focus_controls()` is a shell
  pass-through, so UIR-05's bridge reads them without a screen-owned policy.
- **UIR-22's mount** owns the router registration; the Profile needs nothing from it beyond the
  standard payload (`router_id`, `back_target`, `store`) it already reads.

